Notes on unit 2, per the advisor's catch: the lone `fused` finding's own repair instruction says that when the text after the stop doesn't finish its sentence and the next line opens on a lowercase word, join it down rather than leaving it stranded. `The host authors geometry` doesn't finish its sentence, and the next line opens on `(converted` — lowercase — so c08 (rejoin, then split only at the real sentence boundary, landing under 120 chars) is correct; c09 leaves a fragment line standing alone and is wrong despite looking like the "minimal" fix.
